  "notes": "A compound of {遊|ゆう} (play, leisure) and {歩|ほ} (walk). Most commonly encountered as part of the compound {遊歩道|ゆうほどう} (promenade, walking path/trail), which refers to paved or maintained paths designed for leisurely walking in parks, along riversides, or through scenic areas.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {遊歩道|ゆうほどう}: promenade, walking trail (the most common compound)\n- {遊歩|ゆうほ}コース: walking course, strolling route\n- {森林|しんりん}{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}: forest walking trail\n- {海岸|かいがん}{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}: seaside promenade\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {散歩|さんぽ}: walk, stroll — the everyday word for taking a walk; more common in daily conversation\n- {散策|さんさく}: strolling, rambling — slightly more literary, often used for exploring an area on foot\n- {逍遥|しょうよう}: leisurely walk — literary/archaic, rarely used in modern conversation",
